WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.970
I don't like birds,
I don't like birds.

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.850
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.070
Hi.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.690
My name is Macayla Woodley.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.700
I'm a part of a
big team that train

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.865
animals for "Animal Control."

00:00:16.865 --> 00:00:19.645
This is full
time, so it's busy.

00:00:19.645 --> 00:00:22.420
I'm usually making sure
that every wild animal

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.910
that we're having on
the show is comfortable.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.550
But every animal has
its own different kink

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.740
that you kind of have to
work out and work around.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.139
And you are just
as cute and adorable.

00:00:33.139 --> 00:00:36.400
Bunnies are very
challenging because they only

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.420
care about food.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:40.130
And they are a prey animal,
so everything is scary to them

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:40.930
at first.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:42.530
So you have to work them
through that before you

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:43.750
can even start training them.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:46.558
[YELLS]

00:00:46.558 --> 00:00:49.366
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:50.302 --> 00:00:53.605
The ferret we
had with Michael.

00:00:53.605 --> 00:00:54.670
Bad choice.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:58.220
It was a scene that we had
to put the ferret on his chest.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.820
He was kind of supposed to
pretend to, like, freak out.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.802
[SCREAMS] [LAUGH]

00:01:03.802 --> 00:01:05.400
Just that was fun to watch.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.150
I worked with
a young kangaroo.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.010
I think it was-- he
was a first time actor.

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:10.300
And honestly, it showed.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.740
[GROANS]

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:13.000
It's on me, now.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.200
They wanted to have
python rehearsal,

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.590
which is also the name of a
new movie I have coming out.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:19.765
Does this look like it
would have gotten this way?

00:01:19.765 --> 00:01:21.250
Joel's great with the animals.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:22.180
You got that, kitty cat?

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.950
Actually, everyone on
this show has been good.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.800
And sometimes, that
can be hard with actors

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:29.410
because some of them aren't
as willing to do those things.

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:31.000
Grace was hesitant
about the iguana.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.590
That was the most terrifying.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:34.750
I didn't think I had
a problem with them

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:35.890
until I saw it up close.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:39.130
I'm pretty sure there's
footage of me freaking out.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.100
He doesn't like me.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.290
Oh, my god. (WHIMPERING)
I'm not doing good at all.

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.450
It ended up being
a really great day,

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:51.168
and she warmed up quite quickly.

00:01:51.168 --> 00:01:54.156
[SULTRY MUSIC]

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.410
There's never a dull moment.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.960
It's been the most
amazing experience.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.760
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.360
[MOOS]

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:09.200
[MUSIC CONTINUES]

